AB  - Algorithm innovation is the core of technological contribution. This paper presents three novel algorithms addressing critical limitations in AI-VR integration for interior design: 1) A Style-Constrained Diffusion with Detail Attention (SCDA) algorithm, which introduces a dual-loss mechanism and gradient-weighted sampling to solve style deviation and detail blurriness in scene generation; 2) A Multi-Modal Attention-Immersion Fusion (MAIF) model, leveraging Light GBM with cross-modal feature interaction to capture non-linear relationships between eye-tracking data and immersion; 3) A Priority-Aware Dynamic Scheduling (PADS) algorithm, designed with adaptive resource preemption to optimize real-time performance in multi-module collaboration. Theoretical analysis and experimental results validate the innovations: SCDA improves style accuracy by 16.5% and detail richness by 15.3% over baseline diffusion models; MAIF achieves R2=0.82 (21.2% higher than linear models) in immersion prediction; PADS reduces end-to-end latency by 40% compared to traditional scheduling. These algorithms establish a foundational framework for AI-VR technical integration, with clear theoretical contributions to generative models, attention modeling, and real-time systems.
ER  - 

