AB  - While drones have the potential to serve as embodied AI assistants for everyday tasks, current AI agents demonstrate low task success rates in autonomous flight, limiting real-world applicability. This work-in-progress presents a drone assistant prototype equipped with agentic tools for interaction through Extended Reality (XR), enabling agents to leverage human capabilities to help overcome current limitations. We developed the toolset based on feedback from six participants across three design iterations of a Wizard-Of-Oz probe in outdoor pick-and-place tasks. We then implemented a high-fidelity version using Meta Quest 3, AirSim, and a vision-language model, and evaluated perceived agency and effort through video walkthroughs and surveys. Preliminary results support the feasibility of XR-mediated drone assistance and motivate further evaluation in real-world settings.
