AB  - Traditional virtual reality scene construction methods are cumbersome and inefficient, relying on manual modeling and preset rules, which limits immersive experiences. This paper proposes a digital media VR scene construction method that integrates neural networks, utilizing convolutional neural networks and generative adversarial networks to analyze and generate multimodal data such as images, videos, and voices. A neural network-based 3D modeling automation process, scene texture synthesis algorithm, and user behavior interaction optimization are designed, improving construction efficiency and immersion. Experimental results show that this method significantly outperforms traditional ones in speed, image fidelity, and user experience, with modeling times ranging from 60 to 270 seconds and a structural similarity index improvement of $\mathbf{0. 1 3 - 0. 1 8}$. This research paves the way for intelligent VR system development and future digital content fusion applications.
