AB  - At present, VR scene construction faces the core challenges such as the contradiction between realism and real-time, the difference between static and dynamic scene processing, and the traditional methods have shortcomings in the reconstruction accuracy of complex environment, the completion of occlusion areas and the efficient rendering of mobile terminals. Therefore, this study proposes an intelligent generation framework for VR scenes, which integrates 3D reconstruction and deep learning, and adopts a four-layer heterogeneous pipeline architecture: the data layer processes multi-view images or sparse point clouds through mixed data structures; The intelligent generation layer combines NeRF variant and Latent Diffusion Model (LDM), and solves the problem of occlusion completion through two-stage joint training strategy, and introduces consistency loss function to balance reconstruction accuracy and generation quality. The physical simulation layer realizes dynamic physical coupling based on LSTM prediction and NVIDIA PhysX engine to ensure that the behavior of virtual objects conforms to physical laws; The rendering layer adopts lightweight strategies such as layered rendering and texture compression to support efficient rendering of mobile 4K scenes. The experimental results show that this method performs well on ScanNet v2, industrial self-built data sets and DynamicFAUST data sets: the Chamfer Distance (CD) of 3D reconstruction is reduced to 0.51±0.09cm, the F-score is 93.7%, and the cavity repair rate is increased to 90.3%; At 4K resolution, the frame rate of complex scene rendering reaches 45fps, which is 87.5% higher than that of NeRF-only method. The success rate of physical interaction task is over 93%, and the response delay is controlled within 15ms. This research provides a low-cost and efficient VR scene generation solution for industrial design, virtual production and other fields, and promotes the depth of VR technology in practical application.
ER  - 

