AB  - As AI agents increasingly populate Virtual Reality (VR), evaluating their social norm adherence is critical yet underexplored. We present a Symmetrical Reality testbed benchmarking AI social behaviors across 8 tasks in four norm categories. Evaluation of GPT-5, Gemini 3 Pro, and Qwen3-VL reveals models rely heavily on explicit prompts and struggle with context-dependent norms. A text-only baseline comparison exposes a significant “perception-reasoning gap”: models score higher in textual reasoning (0.64) versus visual-spatial compliance (0.33). This highlights that the primary bottleneck is not lacking social knowledge, but inability to autonomously extract task-relevant visual cues from complex environments.
ER  - 

