AB  - As the power system continues to develop, the application of augmented reality (AR) and 3D reconstruction technologies in power scenarios is becoming increasingly widespread. This paper proposes the integration of these two technologies for the detection, maintenance, and fault diagnosis of power equipment. Through real-time video segmentation and detection operations, AR technology can overlay key information onto the field view, helping engineers quickly identify equipment status and potential issues. Simultaneously, 3D reconstruction technology can generate precise models of power equipment and environments, providing comprehensive visual references and analytical tools that enhance maintenance efficiency and safety. The combined application of these technologies can significantly reduce the risks and costs associated with manual operations.
