AB  - Personalized teaching remains difficult in traditional classrooms due to constraints in teacher capacity, class size, and curricular rigidity. Generative AI (GenAI) and immersive virtual reality (VR) have independently shown positive effects on learning outcomes, yet their deep integration for realtime personalized instruction is underexplored. This paper proposes an AI-Augmented Immersive Learning Environment (AI-ILE) framework comprising three modules: a GenAI-driven content generation engine, a real-time multimodal interaction and feedback engine, and an adaptive personalization module. A quasiexperimental study with 120 undergraduate students shows that AI-ILE significantly outperforms VR-only and GenAI-only baselines in knowledge gain, engagement, personalization effectiveness, and satisfaction. Ablation analysis confirms each module's contribution.
ER  - 

