AB  - The COVID-19 pandemic significantly reshaped university education, fostering a reliance on online learning and recorded lectures that have, for many students, diminished engagement with physical campus life and traditional offline learning. Recognizing the pervasive role of mobile devices in students' daily lives, this paper introduces UniVenture, a novel mobile application designed to rekindle students' connection to campus and enhance their holistic university experience. The application features an AR-driven adventure game that gamifies campus exploration, offering incentives like rewards and discounts to encourage physical engagement. Furthermore, UniVenture enhances academic success through an AI-powered speech-to-text and summarization system for lecture recordings, making educational content more accessible and digestible. Multiple experiments have been conducted to analyze the performance of the used architecture using benchmark datasets.
