AB  - OST HMDs require correcting for the camera-to-eye offset whenever virtual cues are derived from camera imagery. We demonstrate two methods that align these cues with the user’s view by projecting the processed camera image onto a planar proxy: One keeps this plane at a constant depth, which is sufficient when parallax is small but causes misalignments otherwise, the other uses eye-tracking to adjust the plane dynamically to the user’s fixation, preserving alignment as the user shifts focus. We demonstrate the fixed-distance version on Microsoft HoloLens 2 and Snap AR Glasses, and the gaze-driven version on HoloLens 2.
