AB  - We present From Cards to Creatures, a mobile augmented reality system that enables interactive 3D visualization of physical trading cards through generative AI. The proposed pipeline combines object detection, retrieval, and image-to-3D generation to support real-time rendering anchored to physical inputs. Specifically, we use a YOLOv11-based detector to identify and extract the card’s unique ID from the mobile camera feed. This ID allows for the instant retrieval of a corresponding 3D asset from a pre-compiled dataset. To build this dataset, each card’s artwork was processed with the Hunyuan3D-2.1 generative model to produce a high-quality mesh and texture. The retrieved model is then rendered and spatially aligned with the detected card in the AR scene. By decoupling the generation process from real-time image capture, the system ensures consistent reconstruction and low-latency inference. We evaluate the system qualitatively using a set of collectible Pokémon cards, demonstrating accurate alignment, coherent shape generation, and responsiveness during interaction. This case study illustrates a modular architecture that can be extended to other domains involving physical artifacts and generative 3D content.
ER  - 

